1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,869
This is the most important episode in the whole series.

2
00:00:01,869 --> 00:00:05,539
We give the model a tool, and watch it go from answering questions to actually doing things on your machine.

3
00:00:05,539 --> 00:00:07,000
This is the moment a chat becomes an agent.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,162
Open the tools panel on the right of the chat and switch on Files.

5
00:00:10,162 --> 00:00:15,000
That's it — the model can now read and write files, but only where you allow, which is the next step.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,941
When prompted, set a working directory.

7
00:00:16,941 --> 00:00:23,362
This is a hard boundary: the model can only see and touch files inside this folder — nothing above it, nowhere else on your disk.

8
00:00:23,362 --> 00:00:26,000
Point it at a real project you don't mind it reading.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,205
Now the prompt.

10
00:00:27,205 --> 00:00:33,071
Ask it: read the README in this folder and tell me what the project does.

11
00:00:33,071 --> 00:00:35,000
Watch what happens next.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:35,584
Here's the aha.

13
00:00:35,584 --> 00:00:37,338
A tool-call card appears in the conversation.

14
00:00:37,338 --> 00:00:41,545
You can see the call it made, the exact arguments it chose, and the result that came back — all inspectable.

15
00:00:41,545 --> 00:00:44,273
It decided to read the file, read it, and answered from what it found.

16
00:00:44,273 --> 00:00:47,000
That's the call, read, respond loop, and it's the heart of everything.

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:47,724
One crucial gotcha.

18
00:00:47,724 --> 00:00:51,270
Small local models often can't call tools reliably, no matter what their model card promises.

19
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:55,311
If this step fails on a local model, that's almost always the reason — not a misconfiguration on your end.

20
00:00:55,311 --> 00:00:58,056
Before you go debugging, test the exact same prompt with a bigger model.

21
00:00:58,056 --> 00:01:00,000
If it works there, the small model was the problem.

22
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,154
Now you've seen the core idea.

23
00:01:01,154 --> 00:01:06,000
Next we take a proper tour of the sidebar, so the deeper episodes can dive in without stopping to explain where everything is.

